# A character past ASCII inside a sequence ends it. In a CSI or DCS
# header, vtium ignores the sequence up to its final byte. After ESC or
# ESC (, vtium drops the sequence, so the next character prints.
# spec: vt100.net's DEC parser; vtium-parse's README, "A character past ASCII ends a sequence header in UTF-8 mode"
size 10 4
send "\e[1\u{e9}mA\e[m"
send "\e\u{e9}B"
send "\e[\u{4e16}2CC"
send "\e(\u{e9}0D"
send "\eP1\u{e9}q\e\\E"
dump state
